SUMMARY: St. Velveeta Devotional Candle Launch
DESCRIPTION:Candle Launch + Meet & Greet with Saint Velveeta Fondue\n\nFR
 EE Event | 6-8pm | Live Music | All-Ages | Bar w/ID\n\nLive Music by Todd
  Umhoefer\n\nThursday\, May 14th\, The Old Church is proud to present our
  first collaborative merch launch and meet-and-greet feat. Velveeta Fondu
 e!\n\nAs supporters and patrons of The Old Church\, we all carry the flam
 e to unite music\, art\, and community\, and now you can memorialize this
  passion in our first ever Devotional Candle. Claim your flame here\, and
  receive it at the commemorative event May 14th in our Cheshire Lounge (t
 his is a free event\, and candle purchase is not necessary for entry).\n\
 nAt this special launch party\, the Patron Saint of Preservation celebrat
 es her celestial calling with a brief reading followed by gooey\, ambient
  music from clarinetist Todd Umhoefer https://toddumhoefer.bandcamp.com/ 
 . Enjoy snacks and drinks at our bar\, peruse Ash Stone's "Say Cheese!" g
 allery exhibition https://tockify.com/theoldchurch/detail/771/17750268000
 00 \, and mingle with the melty muse herself at this all ages gathering.\
 n\nReserve a piece of history now with this inaugural artist/venue collab
 oration Devotional Candle featuring St. Velveeta Fondue and we will see y
 ou May 14th!\n\nMore on Velveeta: Born in 1916\, Velveeta Fondue resides 
 in the Missouri Cheese Caves\, also known as the Springfield Underground.
  She’s the All-American Big Dairy Heir who never takes a day off work. Ve
 lveeta is made of pasteurized prepared cheese product and preserved to ag
 eless perfection with the finest fillers on this side of the Mississippi.
  A queen of Southern idioms and storytelling\, Ms. Fondue serves as a mus
 e for her daytime persona\, artist Ash Stone.\n\nArtist Bio:\n\nAsh Stone
  (she/they) is a multidisciplinary artist\, photographer\, and educator b
 ased in Portland\,\n\nOregon. Her work\, rooted in play and humor\, serve
 s as both a reclamation of agency and a healing ritual while exploring th
 emes of domestic dysfunction. Ash uses photography\, installation\, exper
 imental short film\, and her drag persona\, Velveeta Fondue\, as tools to
  examine cultural identity and the myth of the “American Dream”. As a bir
 acial Tejano\, Stone draws inspiration from generational knowledge\, the 
 grief process\, and an archive of family photos. Her practice is informed
  by the labor and thinking of intersectional feminists\, psychologists\, 
 scientists\, teachers\, grocery store employees\, and housekeepers. Ash i
 s currently a co-director with time-based artist alliance\, Outer Voice\,
  and educator with Portland Community College. She holds an MFA from the 
 Pacific Northwest College of Art and a BFA from the University of North T
 exas.
CATEGORIES:lunchtime-concerts
